# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# openscad-cli — what must never be committed, and why
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local development toolchain and the OpenSCAD engine stand-in.
# `.tools/` holds a private Node.js runtime and an unpacked ~180 MB OpenSCAD.app
# plus the downloaded .dmg. It is the single largest thing in a working tree and
# must never enter git. It is also disposable: re-created by
# `.tools/env.sh` plus the engine download, and replaced entirely once Homebrew
# can build the pinned engine.
.tools/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `dist/` is emitted by `npm run build` and is reproducible from `src/`.
dist/
# `build/` stages both packaging jobs: the engine (build-engine.sh defaults to
# build/engine) and the AppImage AppDir (build/appimage). Unanchored, so the
# one line covers either of them.
build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# package-lock.json IS committed on purpose: without it `npm ci` is not
# reproducible, and reproducibility is the point of this project.
node_modules/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Engine submodule
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The gitlink under engine/ — the recorded commit SHA — is what pins the
# engine, so /engine/ is deliberately NOT ignored. A rule written here cannot
# reach inside it either: the submodule carries its own .gitignore, and git
# rejects an engine/… pathspec from this file as "in submodule 'engine'".
#
# The patches themselves are source — make-source-tarball.sh ships the whole
# packaging/patches/ tree as part of the corresponding source — so applied/ is
# the one part of it left out.
/packaging/patches/applied/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything the CLI produces at runtime: work directories, sidecar manifests,
# and exported geometry. These are outputs of a model, never inputs.
.openscad-cli/
*.openscad.json
*.stl
*.off
*.obj
*.wrl
*.3mf
*.dxf
*.svg
*.pdf
*.csg
*.ast
*.echo
*.param
*.pov

# ...except small fixtures, which are inputs and belong in version control so
# the import() tests are reproducible. Add fixture assets under
# test/fixtures/assets/ and re-include them here.
!test/fixtures/assets/*.stl
!test/fixtures/assets/*.off
!test/fixtures/assets/*.obj
!test/fixtures/assets/*.svg
!test/fixtures/assets/*.dxf
!test/fixtures/assets/*.3mf

# Scratch models. The README's worked example is one of these — its .scad is
# deliberately kept out of the repo, so the directory scratch models get built
# in is ignored whole, inputs as well as exports: `git add -A` then cannot pull
# a part into a release by accident. A model worth keeping belongs in
# test/fixtures/ with the test that covers it, or in assets/ as documentation.
models/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release artifacts — these are published, not committed.
# Compliance check 9 fails the release if a binary ever lands in git.
*.AppImage
*.dmg
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.wasm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project has no runtime configuration and talks to no service, so there
# is nothing to authenticate against. These entries are defensive: if a future
# change ever needs a token, it must reach the machine and never the repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
.netrc
.npmrc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
